<http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/results/FloodFrequencyValueCode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Code list for FloodFrequencyValue - codelist class"@en .
<http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/results/FloodFrequencyValueCode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/results/FloodFrequencyValueCollection> .
<http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/results/FloodFrequencyValueCode> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Refers to the statistical analysis of the occurrence of floods at a particular location over a defined time period. It often involves calculating the recurrence intervals or return periods of flood events, which are typically used to understand how often a specific flood magnitude (like a 100-year flood) is likely to occur. Source: Introduction to Flood Frequency Analysis" .
