# 
# http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/results/structureGradeValueCode-MO
<http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/results/structureGradeValueCode-MO> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/results/StructureGradeValueCode> .
<http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/results/structureGradeValueCode-MO> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/results/structureGradeValueCode-MO> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/isPartOf> <http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/results/StructureGradeValueCollection> .
<http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/results/structureGradeValueCode-MO> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Aggregates are observable in place and there is a distinct arrangement of natural surfaces of weakness. When disturbed, the soil material breaks into a mixture of many entire aggregates, some broken aggregates, and little material without aggregates faces. Aggregates surfaces generally show distinct differences with the aggregates interiors." .
<http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/results/structureGradeValueCode-MO> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/results/> .
