<http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/results/voidsClassificationValueCode-I> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Controlled by the fabric, or arrangement, of the soil particles, also known as textural voids. Subdivision possible into simple packing voids, which relate to the packing of sand particles, and compound packing voids, which result from the packing of non-accommodating peds. Predominantly irregular in shape and interconnected, and hard to quantify in the field." .
<http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/results/voidsClassificationValueCode-I> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/results/> .
<http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/results/voidsClassificationValueCode-I> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "I" .
<http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/results/voidsClassificationValueCode-I> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Interstitial"@en .
# 
# http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/results/voidsClassificationValueCode-P
<http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/results/voidsClassificationValueCode-P> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://w3id.org/glosis/model/codelists/results/VoidsClassificationValueCode> .
